Maia Chess Extension - Licensing
================================

This extension bundles components under two different licenses. The bundled
files determine which terms apply to them.


1. Maia-3 components: GNU Affero General Public License v3.0
-------------------------------------------------------------

The following are licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 (AGPL-3.0):

  engine/maia/maia3-3m.onnx
  engine/maia/maia3-5m.onnx
  engine/maia/maia3-encoder.js
  engine/maia/maia3-moves.js

The bundled ONNX networks are fp16 exports of Maia3-5M and the Maia3 3M
ablation, converted for the browser by bqrio/maia3-onnx. The reference
implementation is CSSLab/maia3. Both carry the AGPL-3.0 licence:

  Model:   https://huggingface.co/UofTCSSLab/Maia3-5M
  ONNX:    https://huggingface.co/bqrio/maia3-onnx
  Source:  https://github.com/CSSLab/maia3

Why this matters: the AGPL extends its source-availability requirement to
conveying the software over a network. A packaged build of this extension
therefore carries the corresponding-source obligations for these components.
The corresponding source is this repository, together with the upstream
Maia-3 sources linked above. The encoder and move-map files in
engine/maia/ are derived from the upstream tokenizer and move vocabulary
and are original implementations of them; the accompanying Python reference
that generates the test expectations for them uses the upstream tokenizer
directly.


2. Runtime and engine components: MIT and MIT-licensed Stockfish
----------------------------------------------------------------

  engine/maia/ort/            onnxruntime-web, MIT
                              https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
  engine/stockfish.js and
  engine/sf171-*.js/.wasm     Stockfish, GPL-3.0-or-later
  engine/nn-*.nnue,
  engine/stockfish-nnue-*     Stockfish NNUE, GPL-3.0-or-later
                              https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish

  src/                        extension source. See the note below.


Note on the extension's own source
----------------------------------
The extension's own JavaScript, HTML and CSS in src/ are not covered by a
licence file in this repository. Stockfish is GPL-3.0-or-later and is linked
into this extension, and the Maia-3 components above are AGPL-3.0, so the
combined distributed work must be released under terms compatible with both
before it is redistributed. AGPL-3.0 is compatible with GPL-3.0 and is the
stricter of the two, so AGPL-3.0 is a safe choice for the combined work.
This file records that obligation; it is not a completed licence grant for
the whole repository.

If you redistribute this extension as a binary or a download, you must offer
the complete corresponding source for the AGPL- and GPL-licensed components,
which this repository satisfies for the Maia-3 code and the upstream Maia-3
sources it links.


Upstream copyright
------------------
Maia-3:      Copyright (c) the Maia-3 authors, CSSLab, University of Toronto
Stockfish:   Copyright (c) the Stockfish authors
onnxruntime: Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation

Maia was created for research into human-like chess play. The bundled weights
were trained on human game data. Use responsibly: this extension is intended
for post-game review and training, not for cheating in rated games.
